{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts","id":1406170,"title":"Trying to understand ghosts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-03T16:27:52-07:00","id":1406170,"title":"Trying to understand ghosts","content":"I have some doubts on whether I understand the ghosts in Exalted correctly. <br /> <br /> 1 PO ghosts - these seem simple. Perpetually angry. Usually walk in Creation, immaterial unless they materialise. Get killed by direct sunlight. Bound to their body.<br /> <br /> 2 HUN ghosts - the actual 'mind' of the dead person. When in the realm of the dead, or in shadowlands, they are material and interact with stuff normally. <br /> <br /> Now what I want to make sure is how they interact with Creation outside shadowlands. <br /> I take it they are usually immaterial, and few of them have means to materialise. <br /> <br /> - Do they need to find a shadowland to enter creation? If yes, do they need to come back to it before sunrise or is sunlight not a problem for them?<br /> - Can they interact with mortals without directly entering Creation (show up in dreams and such)? <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","name":"Braininthejar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T16:32:22-07:00","id":1406172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Braininthejar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts#post1406170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Do they need to find a shadowland to enter creation? If yes, do they need to come back to it before sunrise or is sunlight not a problem for them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no. Not all ghosts go directly to the Underworld. Some stick around in Creation. How and when this happens is entirely ST whim.<br /> <br /> If a ghost is in the Underworld? Then the default is a shadowland. There can be some exceptions (spells), but a shadowland is the default.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Braininthejar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts#post1406170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Can they interact with mortals without directly entering Creation (show up in dreams and such)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see why not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T16:49:57-07:00","id":1406177,"title":"","content":"Your avatar is super apropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","name":"Braininthejar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T17:13:42-07:00","id":1406185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Braininthejar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts#post1406170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Do they need to find a shadowland to enter creation? If yes, do they need to come back to it before sunrise or is sunlight not a problem for them?</div> </div> </div> </div>The best information we have at this time is still from 2nd edition. According to the Roll of Glorious Divinity 2 and CoCD: The Underworld, ghosts manifest in the Underworld, usually in the place equivalent to where they died or where they were buried, so to enter Creation they need to use a shadowland or some other magical means. Ghosts do not have a problem with sunlight directly, though their grave goods are destroyed by the light of the Unconquered Sun.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Can they interact with mortals without directly entering Creation (show up in dreams and such)? </div> </div> </div>Yes. The Arcanos called Honored Ancestor's Ways contained a Charm called Courier In Dreams, which allowed a ghost to send 50 word messages to a descendant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T17:24:52-07:00","id":1406186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts?p=1406185#post1406185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The best information we have at this time is still from 2nd edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>If by &quot;best information&quot; you mean &quot;best information about what will be published in future Third Edition material,&quot; this statement is false here, and is generally false when used elsewhere. I say this as a line developer responsible for making decisions about what inspiration we draw from First and Second Edition material. First Edition sources almost always take priority over Second Edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T17:56:43-07:00","id":1406192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Braininthejar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts#post1406170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perpetually angry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not true; a po soul usually becomes a vengeful hungry ghost if the body wasn't given a proper burial.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Braininthejar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts#post1406170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Usually walk in Creation</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Usually </i>stays with the body, unless it becomes a hungry ghost.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Braininthejar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts#post1406170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">immaterial unless they materialise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, per their writeup, they dematerialize when they go to inhabit the body.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Braininthejar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts#post1406170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the actual 'mind' of the dead person.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would describe the Hun soul more as the seat of <i>most of</i> the dead person's memories and identity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Braininthejar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts#post1406170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When in the realm of the dead, or in shadowlands, they are material and interact with stuff normally.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is accurate, except they're only naturally material in shadowlands <i>at night</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Braininthejar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts#post1406170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I take it they are usually immaterial, and few of them have means to materialise.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is correct; for instance, honored ancestors and war-ghosts need other ways to interact with Creation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Braininthejar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts#post1406170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do they need to find a shadowland to enter creation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Braininthejar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts#post1406170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If yes, do they need to come back to it before sunrise or is sunlight not a problem for them?</div> </div> </div> </div>We don't know the full answer to this one yet; there's been no indication yet that ghosts suffer any negative effects in the sun (other than, in previous editions, its light destroying grave goods).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Braininthejar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts#post1406170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can they interact with mortals without directly entering Creation (show up in dreams and such)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine there'll be Charms to allow for such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 08-04-2020, 03:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T23:46:11-07:00","id":1406229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts?p=1406186#post1406186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If by &quot;best information&quot; you mean &quot;best information about what will be published in future Third Edition material,&quot; this statement is false here, and is generally false when used elsewhere. I say this as a line developer responsible for making decisions about what inspiration we draw from First and Second Edition material. First Edition sources almost always take priority over Second Edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>The best information we have is from... *examines pile of books*... Exalted the Abyssals and the Book of Bone and Ebony <i>which say exactly the same thing as their 2E counterparts</i>.<br /> <br /> I realise you want to protect the intellectual integrity of your art, but this thread is about helping a new player understand the gameline. It's great that you want to interact with the community, and the last thing I want is to return to the old WW forums cussing out writers and developers to their face. But of all of us, you are uniquely positioned to help Braininthejar understand Exalted. You're not obligated to help them, but you'd be a lot cooler if you did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T08:29:38-07:00","id":1406275,"title":"","content":"&quot;The best information we have at this time is still from 2nd edition&quot; is repeatedly used on the forum as a universal statement applying to all things, and countering that is absolutely important to helping players understand the direction of the Third Edition line. I am trying to be helpful, not to &quot;protect the intellectual integrity of [my] art.&quot;<br /> <br /> If the 1e and 2e material is absolutely identical here (which I doubt, but I do not have the time to check), then no harm is done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T09:43:10-07:00","id":1406285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts?p=1406275#post1406275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;The best information we have at this time is still from 2nd edition&quot; is repeatedly used on the forum as a universal statement applying to all things, and countering that is absolutely important to helping players understand the direction of the Third Edition line. I am trying to be helpful, not to &quot;protect the intellectual integrity of [my] art.&quot;<br /> <br /> If the 1e and 2e material is absolutely identical here (which I doubt, but I do not have the time to check), then no harm is done.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Respectfully, if a person is asking a question, the information that is available right now is a bit more useful than the information that will be available in the future.<br /> <br /> I expect and even hope for quite a few revisions to the unquiet dead when the game can get to it, but neither I nor anybody else can use that to answer a person's questions today.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T09:46:58-07:00","id":1406286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts?p=1406285#post1406285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Respectfully, if a person is asking a question, the information that is available right now is a bit more useful than the information that will be available in the future.<br /> <br /> I expect and even hope for quite a few revisions to the unquiet dead when the game can get to it, but neither I nor anybody else can use that to answer a person's questions today.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but if there's two available sets of information right now and one that will be available in the future, and one of the two sets of information will comport more closely to the one that will be available in the future, then informing the person with the inquiry about which one that will be is still valuable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T09:47:54-07:00","id":1406287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts?p=1406285#post1406285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Respectfully, if a person is asking a question, the information that is available right now is a bit more useful than the information that will be available in the future.<br /> <br /> I expect and even hope for quite a few revisions to the unquiet dead when the game can get to it, but neither I nor anybody else can use that to answer a person's questions today.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sure, but &quot;as a general rule, please refer to 1E material rather than using information from 2E&quot; is what Eric said, not &quot;this question will be answered later in the line's lifecycle&quot;.<br /> <br /> Edit: wow, ninja'd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T10:29:12-07:00","id":1406292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts?p=1406229#post1406229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The best information we have is from... *examines pile of books*... Exalted the Abyssals and the Book of Bone and Ebony <i>which say exactly the same thing as their 2E counterparts</i>.<br /> <br /> I realise you want to protect the intellectual integrity of your art, but this thread is about helping a new player understand the gameline. It's great that you want to interact with the community, and the last thing I want is to return to the old WW forums cussing out writers and developers to their face. But of all of us, you are uniquely positioned to help Braininthejar understand Exalted. You're not obligated to help them, but you'd be a lot cooler if you did.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Don't lecture other posters</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T10:38:58-07:00","id":1406295,"title":"","content":"Also, to be clear, if someone wants to know what's their best source for <i>a larger quantity</i> of information on a topic <i>now</i> without regard for whether it will match up with Third Edition's future direction, then &quot;2e has more to say on this topic than 1e and can thus provide you with a larger quantity of information than 1e&quot; is absolutely a useful response! But that did not seem to be the question being asked, and it did not seem to be the thrust of the answer that I was commenting on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T11:00:16-07:00","id":1406296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts?p=1406186#post1406186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If by &amp;quot;best information&amp;quot; you mean &amp;quot;best information about what will be published in future Third Edition material,&amp;quot; this statement is false here, and is generally false when used elsewhere. I say this as a line developer responsible for making decisions about what inspiration we draw from First and Second Edition material. First Edition sources almost always take priority over Second Edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. So just to clarify, if I wanted to anticipate like what Sidereals will be like in 3e, I\u2019m better off reading Sidereals 1e than Sidereals 2e?<br /> <br /> Not an academic question. I actually do wanna buy some old Exalted books and I don\u2019t want to buy the wrong stuff. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T11:13:58-07:00","id":1406304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts?p=1406296#post1406296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay. So just to clarify, if I wanted to anticipate like what Sidereals will be like in 3e, I\u2019m better off reading Sidereals 1e than Sidereals 2e?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, with the caveat that there will still be significant differences.<br /> <br /> (We should probably get back to talking about ghosts!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T12:23:19-07:00","id":1406314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts?p=1406304#post1406304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(We should probably get back to talking about ghosts!)</div> </div> </div> </div>Something else to note about ghosts is that they\u2019re probably the spookiest things in creation. Other things may be scarier, but for straight up spoop factor ghosts are at least contenders for top a lot. <br /> <br /> While Hungry Ghosts who hunt at night and War Ghosts who possess armor are certainly good examples of what ghosts might do, most things from Ghostbusters and Poltergeist are also on the table for ways they can interact with the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T14:57:37-07:00","id":1406333,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1120_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1120\" data-vbnamecard=\"1120\">Eric Minton</a> Sorry lol<br /> <br /> But thank you","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T16:24:12-07:00","id":1406347,"title":"","content":"One thing that has crossed my mind at times is that 3e system of Intimacies seems to gel much better with the idea of ghostly fetters than tying them to Virtues as in previous editions ever did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T02:43:11-07:00","id":1406404,"title":"","content":"The Third Edition core's description of the Underworld creates complications to the question of where ghosts end up, as that world no longer maps at all to the land of the living.<br /> <br /> I propose that the rivers be involved; that the soul drifts down into the darkness and awakens to find itself being carried along the currents, watching helpless as many countries drift by and trying not to be submerged; there's no drowning, but they'll see things down there they'll wish they hadn't. Most commonly, they'll eventually be washed on the banks of a place that, by its nature and its Laws, is most fitting to their situation, by criteria that are often self-evident but frequently mysterious (but scholars of the dead are reasonably certain are never arbitrary).<br /> <br /> But the banks of the dead are often occupied, and some ghosts are called ashore by music and lights to take part, and the rivers are often plied by boats that will pull stray souls aboard. There are those who'll pull people up as a refuge, but many more who lay out nets to sweep up ghosts destined for the soulforges, moliation or even just being placed at the service of some magnate of the dark lands.<br /> <br /> And an unlucky or cursed few are never cast up or caught; they stay trapped in the current until it carries them all the way to the Stygian well. There many will be collected by the snares of the Labyrinth and the nephwracks, and those that aren't will finally be carried to the endless darkness, and ghosts will debate among themselves which is a worse fate.<br /> <br /> The experience varies slightly depending on how fine one's funeral was; plenty of ghosts find themselves in vessels modelled after their burial suits or vessels that make the journey more comfortable and safer. If a riding animal was pledged to you, it will likely rise up beneath you now and just this once be permitted to walk along the surface of the river waters until it reaches your destination. Most fortunate of all are those whose grave goods included an actual boat, as they not only get to enter the Underworld in style, they actually get a greater measure of agency about where they first end up than most do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T05:57:45-07:00","id":1406418,"title":"","content":"Sounds kind of like the Egyptian or Greek underworld actually. I\u2019ll have to reread that section.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T12:47:59-07:00","id":1406492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts?p=1406404#post1406404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Third Edition core's description of the Underworld creates complications to the question of where ghosts end up, as that world no longer maps at all to the land of the living.</div> </div> </div> </div>No? could you point out the references that support this? I probably missed them and now feel curious on the subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T13:05:43-07:00","id":1406496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts?p=1406492#post1406492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No? could you point out the references that support this? I probably missed them and now feel curious on the subject.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The big one in print is the Underworld section in the core book, where it describes the Underworld as &quot;a great confluence of dead waterways. It teems with oceans of void and rivers of darkness, flowing ever away from Creation [...] These tempest-wracked seas and black torrents divide the strange islets of the Underworld\u2014a multitude of paradises, purgatories, and stranger afterlives&quot; (Exalted, p. 114). Since Creation is <i>not</i> a confluence of dead waterways, or composed of a multitude of strange islets, it follows that the Underworld can't resemble Creation too closely. From various dev comments, we know that shadowlands resemble Creation, and that the further you get from a shadowland, the less Creation-y the Underworld becomes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T13:12:59-07:00","id":1406497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts?p=1406492#post1406492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No? could you point out the references that support this? I probably missed them and now feel curious on the subject.</div> </div> </div> </div>He's not the only one who got that impression. Take a look in my signature for what sort of Underworld I got out of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T17:33:33-07:00","id":1406528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts?p=1406497#post1406497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He's not the only one who got that impression. Take a look in my signature for what sort of Underworld I got out of it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I doubt not, just would like a little nudge toward what parts of the corebook to look for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts?p=1406496#post1406496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The big one in print is the Underworld section in the core book, where it describes the Underworld as &quot;a great confluence of dead waterways. It teems with oceans of void and rivers of darkness, flowing ever away from Creation [...] These tempest-wracked seas and black torrents divide the strange islets of the Underworld\u2014a multitude of paradises, purgatories, and stranger afterlives&quot; (Exalted, p. 114). Since Creation is <i>not</i> a confluence of dead waterways, or composed of a multitude of strange islets, it follows that the Underworld can't resemble Creation too closely. From various dev comments, we know that shadowlands resemble Creation, and that the further you get from a shadowland, the less Creation-y the Underworld becomes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm, sounding a little closer to Wraith in a stealthy way that i find interesting. Nice, nice...<br /> <br /> Also gives off an impression of shadowlands as little isles of stability mirroring Creation and the farther you go, more oniric, like a endless middlemarch of dead titans dreams molded here and there by prayer, human and inhuman, through the ages. At least my own fancy thoughts out of your own commentaries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 08-05-2020, 08:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T17:54:27-07:00","id":1406535,"title":"","content":"As far as I know of Wraith's Underworld, it's fairly contiguous once you get past the... what is it called, the Tempest?<br /> <br /> A multitude of dead dominions separated by rivers seems to me much closer in character to the Underworld of Chronicles of Darkness as most prominently represented in Geist: the Sin-Eaters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T18:11:49-07:00","id":1406540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts?p=1406528#post1406528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I doubt not, just would like a little nudge toward what parts of the corebook to look for.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the description of the Underworld on page 114.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T20:55:57-07:00","id":1406574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts?p=1406229#post1406229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The best information we have is from... *examines pile of books*... Exalted the Abyssals and the Book of Bone and Ebony <i>which say exactly the same thing as their 2E counterparts</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not actually true, the fact people don't recognise the slight setting creep over first edition and assume they didn't notice it earlier is one of the worst aspects of 2E.<br /> <br /> Here\u2019s one example of a change that caused issues for my group.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exalted the Abyssals page 28</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Falling into Oblivion is a very real possibility when facing the Deathlords, the nephwracks or their servants. Soulsteel weapons, the attacks of some monstrous entities and certain Charms can inflict this horrible fate on a ghost, as can being thrown into the Mouth of the Abyss. A ghost who falls into Oblivion is gone. No trace of his soul remains, no fragment of his memory or self is retained.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Role of Glorious Divinity 2 page 95</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Certain Exalted Charms are also capable of completely destroying a ghost, eliminating any possibility of reformation. Generally, such Charms send the ghost directly into Lethe, except for Abyssal Charms, which usually send them into Oblivion.</div> </div> </div> </div>The ruling on charms like Ghost-Eating Technique in the latter paragraph doesn\u2019t exist in first edition and one of my players hated it because and I quote \u201cit creates an incentive to blast Patrick Swayze with a proton gun rather than help him resolve his unfinished business\u201d.<br /> <br /> If the current developers decide they agree with her, this is an example of 2E not having the best information on the subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T23:22:31-07:00","id":1406585,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I\u2019m pretty much puzzled on why I should do the typical \u201cFigure out a ghost\u2019s business\u201d when I can just GET them into Lethe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T23:45:03-07:00","id":1406587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts?p=1406585#post1406585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I\u2019m pretty much puzzled on why I should do the typical \u201cFigure out a ghost\u2019s business\u201d when I can just GET them into Lethe.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Maybe you just want them to chill out a bit and stop making the floor bleed blood that runs up the walls so they become a guardian spirit who aids the community with their ghost powers instead terrorizing it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T23:45:12-07:00","id":1406588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts?p=1406574#post1406574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The ruling on charms like Ghost-Eating Technique in the latter paragraph doesn\u2019t exist in first edition and one of my players hated it because and I quote \u201cit creates an incentive to blast Patrick Swayze with a proton gun rather than help him resolve his unfinished business\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't really play 1e, but I feel like a lot of problems like this existed in 2e. For example the Ebon Dragon's Flaw of Invulnerability is that he couldn't use it against Holy charms, and if the Sun dies...no more Holy. So what to do? Do you work with Heaven to ascend a new god to the throne? Can it be a Solar? Who is worthy? Who would Creation accept? This needs to happen before we can even think about moving against The Ebon Dragon.<br /> <br /> Actually it doesn't. Every Solar just got a free dot of essence and 10 free charms, and there's a charm with no pre-requisite charms called Should the Sun Not Rise where you ignore the fact that the Sun is dead for the purposes of Holy charms, and can use them at discount too.<br /> <br /> <br /> In my opinion charms should fix problems like &quot;This door is locked and I want to be on the other side of it&quot; or &quot;I'm at the bottom of this sheer cliff and I want to be at the top&quot; or &quot;I want to know if this guy sitting across from me intends to murder me in the next few moments&quot; not so much &quot;the progenitor of the very concept of things which are holy, and things which are dark has been taken from this world, and with it one of the greatest weapons we had against this vile enemy, I want that weapon back&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T23:59:46-07:00","id":1406590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts?p=1406574#post1406574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not actually true</div> </div> </div> </div>OP asked a question. Kyeudo said:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts?p=1406185#post1406185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ghosts manifest in the Underworld, usually in the place equivalent to where they died or where they were buried, so to enter Creation they need to use a shadowland or some other magical means. Ghosts do not have a problem with sunlight directly, though their grave goods are destroyed by the light of the Unconquered Sun.<br /> <br /> The Arcanos called Honored Ancestor's Ways contained a Charm called Courier In Dreams, which allowed a ghost to send 50 word messages to a descendant.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is exactly what the Book of Bone and Ebony and Exalted The Abyssals says. Ghosts manifest in the equivalent place to were they died, need a shadowland to enter Creation (or some other magical means), aren't harmed by sunlight (except Hungry Ghosts, who in 1E are destroyed by sunlight <i>outside of a Shadowland</i> unless they rest inside their corpse), their grave goods are destroyed by sunlight, the Arconi Honored Ancestor's Ways contained a Charm called Courier In Dreams to let ghosts communicate with the living.<br /> <br /> You're right that there are setting differences between editions. Minton is right that if someone wants more information, 1E is the place to look. Isator is right in that 3E has changed the presentation of the Underworld significantly.<br /> <br /> But Courier In Dreams is practically a copy-paste job, and I object to the nonsequitor of quoting accurate 1E information and saying &quot;that's not true because 2E is different&quot;. You may as well say &quot;1E had dice adding Charms like 'Wise Arrow' but 2E changed them to generic Excellencies&quot;: you'd be right, but it's nothing to do with what braininthejar or Kyeudo posted.<br /> <br /> If you change the first line of what Kyeudo wrote to &quot;The best information we have is from 1E in Exalted the Abyssals and The Book of Bone and Ebony&quot; then the entire rest of that post is completely accurate.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, I greatly appreciate Lioness taking the time to explicitly point out a difference between 2E and 1E -- I think <i>that's</i> really helpful. (And I wouldn't have lectured Minton over that post as it now stands, cropped down to just the erroneous statement.)<br /> <br /> And I also hope GET yeets ghosts into Oblivion in 3E. [Edit] But I see no reason to devote word-count to this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 08-06-2020, 07:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T00:48:18-07:00","id":1406594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts?p=1406590#post1406590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I also hope GET yeets ghosts into Oblivion in 3E.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I hope that the desire to explicate that sort of thing continues to be suppressed for the duration of the gameline, because engaging in this weird navel-gazing is exactly the kind of book-bloating empty metaphysics nonsense that makes me cringe when going through 2e books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 08-06-2020, 03:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T01:35:01-07:00","id":1406596,"title":"","content":"So does Ghost-Eating Technique in 3e just destroys the ghost ? Does it send them into Oblivion ? Or does it not matter at all ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T02:51:21-07:00","id":1406603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts?p=1406596#post1406596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So does Ghost-Eating Technique in 3e just destroys the ghost? Does it send them into Oblivion?</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn\u2019t say that it sends them to Oblivion or Lethe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts?p=1406596#post1406596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or does it not matter at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d say it\u2019s less that the answer doesn\u2019t matter, and more that there\u2019s not really a way for characters in-setting to know the definitive answer.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s sort of akin to the reasoning for \u201cWhat\u2019s the deal with the Unconquered Sun?\u201d being left vague in 3e; unless your game\u2019s going to be <i>about</i> that, the answer\u2019s not really going to do anything for the players, and having the answer printed in the book makes some STs less inclined to explore it (when their own answer might have been more interesting).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 08-06-2020, 06:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T04:03:04-07:00","id":1406608,"title":"","content":"Third Edition thus far has introduced a 3rd fate for ghosts in the Susurrus write-up, which is where they're not sent to Lethe or Oblivion but are too badly damaged to go on existing as the individual they were.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T04:48:25-07:00","id":1406610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts?p=1406594#post1406594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I hope that the desire to explicate that sort of thing continues to be suppressed for the duration of the gameline, because engaging in this weird navel-gazing is exactly the kind of book-bloating empty metaphysics nonsense that makes me cringe when going through 2e books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I was unclear.<br /> <br /> I am perfectly happy with the way Ghost Eating Technique is written and am desirous that this not be expanded on.<br /> <br /> I don't think that expanding on the game's metaphysics is always bad, but in this case I think it's better to leave it unsaid.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts?p=1406596#post1406596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So does Ghost-Eating Technique in 3e just destroys the ghost ? Does it send them into Oblivion ? Or does it not matter at all ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is a great thing for Introduce A Fact to settle, if it's relevant to your game and the characters have some means of knowing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 08-06-2020, 07:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T05:26:04-07:00","id":1406615,"title":"","content":"I'm okay with it having no clear answer I was just wondering if there was a canonical one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T06:50:35-07:00","id":1406626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts?p=1406588#post1406588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't really play 1e, but I feel like a lot of problems like this existed in 2e. For example the Ebon Dragon's Flaw of Invulnerability is that he couldn't use it against Holy charms, and if the Sun dies...no more Holy. So what to do? Do you work with Heaven to ascend a new god to the throne? Can it be a Solar? Who is worthy? Who would Creation accept? This needs to happen before we can even think about moving against The Ebon Dragon.<br /> <br /> Actually it doesn't. Every Solar just got a free dot of essence and 10 free charms, and there's a charm with no pre-requisite charms called Should the Sun Not Rise where you ignore the fact that the Sun is dead for the purposes of Holy charms, and can use them at discount too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Freelance writers trying to retcon each others content with no meaningful oversight unfortunately goes back to 1st edition<br /> <br /> To keep things topical on the matter of ghosts. Fertile Soul Endowment, the charm which allowed ghosts to sire children was first introduced in the Exalted Player\u2019s Guide and subsequently \u201cclarified\u201d as not working for Deathlords in Exalted: the Autocthonians.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T08:03:33-07:00","id":1406636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts?p=1406596#post1406596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So does Ghost-Eating Technique in 3e just destroys the ghost ? Does it send them into Oblivion ? Or does it not matter at all ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Going by the 3E wording I am pretty sure that technique name is literal, we rip their very existence to shreds and then devour the slaughtered remains of their existence into our anima and use it to regain motes. It seems like a fair conclusion to draw that they aren't going to either Oblivion or Lethe if they get destroyed that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T11:50:17-07:00","id":1406652,"title":"","content":"How is &quot;sent to Oblivion&quot; different from &quot;Destroyed&quot;? Isn't Oblivion a state of permanent non-existence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","name":"Braininthejar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T12:19:54-07:00","id":1406655,"title":"","content":"Yeah, &quot;Oblivion&quot;, capital-O, isn't really a thing in 3e any more. It's not a place. It's just the state of not existing at all, all continuity of existence ended. So I don't think there's any metaphysical difference between saying that Ghost-Eating Technique completely destroys a ghost and saying that it sends them to oblivion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T01:17:21-07:00","id":1406730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts?p=1406585#post1406585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I\u2019m pretty much puzzled on why I should do the typical \u201cFigure out a ghost\u2019s business\u201d when I can just GET them into Lethe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Compassion.<br /> <br /> I should even think that being able to tell ghosts that you can skip over everything and send them on if they dig in their heels could help prevent some from being too stubborn about it, if there's a touch of ruthlessness to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T07:36:40-07:00","id":1406768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts?p=1406596#post1406596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So does Ghost-Eating Technique in 3e just destroys the ghost ? Does it send them into Oblivion ? Or does it not matter at all ?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no more uppercase-O Oblivion in 3e. We already have the Neverborn as vast and dreadful powers seeking the end of all things; making them figureheads for the <i>real</i> vast and dreadful power seeking the end of all things does them a disservice. Lowercase-o &quot;oblivion&quot; addresses the bleak terror of nonexistence.<br /> <br /> Lethe is a peaceful transition, and the Solar Exalted already have social tools to ease ghosts along the way. Ghost-Eating Technique is not one of those tools. Even if you could soothe them unto reincarnation by punching, you're not going to do it by ripping them to shreds and sucking on the remnants like a half-empty juice box.<br /> <br /> (Note the text of Ghost-Eating Technique: &quot;If a spirit is slain by this attack, it is destroyed permanently.&quot; Ghosts are spirits, and &quot;destroyed permanently&quot; doesn't leave any room for reincarnation.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T07:51:32-07:00","id":1406774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts?p=1406768#post1406768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's no more uppercase-O Oblivion in 3e. We already have the Neverborn as vast and dreadful powers seeking the end of all things; making them figureheads for the <i>real</i> vast and dreadful power seeking the end of all things does them a disservice. Lowercase-o &amp;quot;oblivion&amp;quot; addresses the bleak terror of nonexistence.</div> </div> </div> </div>So this is how I figured it would be, but how does this jive with text of six demon binding scabbard from single point. The charm states the creator(Eternal Nova) used the charm to cut his way out of oblivion. How do you cut your way out of non-existence? If Oblivion was like the Phantom Zone I could understand but countering not existing? Is this just legend talking here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T07:54:28-07:00","id":1406776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arkayriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts?p=1406774#post1406774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So this is how I figured it would be, but how does this jive with text of six demon binding scabbard from single point. The charm states the creator(Eternal Nova) used the charm to cut his way out of oblivion. How do you cut your way out of non-existence? If Oblivion was like the Phantom Zone I could understand but countering not existing? Is this just legend talking here?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's some combination of &quot;it's a legend,&quot; &quot;maybe that does mean something if you want it to in your game,&quot; and &quot;it's a core book error.&quot; Take your pick!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T07:56:17-07:00","id":1406777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts?p=1406776#post1406776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's some combination of &amp;quot;it's a legend,&amp;quot; &amp;quot;maybe that does mean something if you want it to in your game,&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;it's a core book error.&amp;quot; Take your pick!</div> </div> </div> </div>Haha ok thanks that works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T08:06:34-07:00","id":1406781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts?p=1406768#post1406768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's no more uppercase-O Oblivion in 3e. We already have the Neverborn as vast and dreadful powers seeking the end of all things; making them figureheads for the <i>real</i> vast and dreadful power seeking the end of all things does them a disservice. Lowercase-o &quot;oblivion&quot; addresses the bleak terror of nonexistence.<br /> <br /> Lethe is a peaceful transition, and the Solar Exalted already have social tools to ease ghosts along the way. Ghost-Eating Technique is not one of those tools. Even if you could soothe them unto reincarnation by punching, you're not going to do it by ripping them to shreds and sucking on the remnants like a half-empty juice box.<br /> <br /> (Note the text of Ghost-Eating Technique: &quot;If a spirit is slain by this attack, it is destroyed permanently.&quot; Ghosts are spirits, and &quot;destroyed permanently&quot; doesn't leave any room for reincarnation.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the answer. <br /> <br /> Still a few questions about it : Does GET destroys permanently &quot;any&quot; spirit killed by it ? (Gods, demons, elementals, no matter their power). I'm also indecisive in considering this technique is basically evil (it simply and purely destroys a soul, which are apparently in limited number in Creation) or not (it's one of the first Charm of the Solar, usually the good guys, at least when you look the other starter Charms in many abilities). Any advice on how to handle it ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T08:39:19-07:00","id":1406786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts?p=1406781#post1406781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does GET destroys permanently &quot;any&quot; spirit killed by it ? (Gods, demons, elementals, no matter their power).</div> </div> </div> </div>This is how the Exalted slew the enemies of the gods, and they became Neverborn rather than utterly ceasing to exist, which suggests some sort of fuzzy limit? But in general, it permanently destroys spirits because that's what it says in the Charm description. Unless and until we elaborate further in printed material, any limits on that are up to the Storyteller.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts?p=1406781#post1406781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also indecisive in considering this technique is basically evil (it simply and purely destroys a soul, which are apparently in limited number in Creation)</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't recall any statements to that effect in 3e. (I'm not sure there were any such statements in previous editions either; all that comes to mind is the limited number of souls in Autochthonia, which isn't Creation.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts?p=1406781#post1406781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any advice on how to handle it ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Discuss it out of character with the whole player group if anyone wants to buy the Charm, in case the players themselves have strong conflicting opinions that will interfere with actual play. Exalted itself takes no explicit moral stances, only aiming to present meaningful situations engaging to the viewpoints that the players themselves bring to the table \u2014 whether their own views, or characters' views they're using as alternate lenses through which to engage with the setting. If a player or character sees destroying a spirit as evil in a way that killing a person is not, then that's their view, and the published setting will not tell them no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T08:41:48-07:00","id":1406787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts?p=1406781#post1406781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does GET destroys permanently &quot;any&quot; spirit killed by it ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. That's its purpose. As the charm itself notes, it was used to kill the primordials in the War of the Gods, and it can certainly kill all other spirits as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also indecisive in considering this technique is basically evil (it simply and purely destroys a soul, which are apparently in limited number in Creation) or not (it's one of the first Charm of the Solar, usually the good guys, at least when you look the other starter Charms in many abilities). Any advice on how to handle it ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Like most Exalted charms, and in fact most tools in general, its morality isn't inherent, but rather depends on the use you put it to. There's a lot of spirits, including some ghosts, where if you &quot;kill&quot; them (i.e. reduce them to incapacitated with lethal damage) they'll simply reform at a latter time, angry at you and wanting to take revenge. If a monstrous ghost is preying on the inhabitants of a village, devouring their souls and flesh, is it evil to destroy it in such a way that you ensure it can never return, rather than temporarily inconvenience it?<br /> <br /> One of Exalted's big themes is exploring the difference between being a powerful protagonist of an epic story, and being a <i>good person</i>. The game <i>wants</i> you to explore that question, to ask &quot;If I was given all this incredible power, how would I use it. What is a moral way to do so?&quot; In order to facilitate that question, the charms can't be designed with an imposed morality. This isn't D&amp;D 3rd, with an alignment system, where spells can come with a [Good] or [Evil] tag that assures you that using them is always in line with the relevant moral stance. Whether or not you use Ghost-Eating Technique only to permanently defeat monstrous spirits who would otherwise return again to prey on you or the innocent, or whether you use it to rip asunder the higher souls of humans who were only doing their job when that brought them into conflict with you, is entirely up to the player, who must make the decision.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T08:42:09-07:00","id":1406788,"title":"","content":"(I lie, the game does take some explicit moral stances. But that's generally where we need to counter ongoing real-world apologia for stuff like empire, racism, and slavery. And that's less &quot;this is an evil thing in-game&quot; and more &quot;we want to be clear about the actual effects these things have on real people in real life.&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T09:05:30-07:00","id":1406791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts?p=1406786#post1406786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is how the Exalted slew the enemies of the gods, and they became Neverborn rather than utterly ceasing to exist, which suggests some sort of fuzzy limit? But in general, it permanently destroys spirits because that's what it says in the Charm description. Unless and until we elaborate further in printed material, any limits on that are up to the Storyteller.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wanted to make sure I didn't miss anything since the Charm is at Essence 1, and I figured killing the greatest spirits could ask for specific conditions that would have more pre-requisites.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1533_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1533\" data-vbnamecard=\"1533\">Kelly Pedersen</a> I don't want to tag it, but I'm looking for insight of the meaning of &quot;definitively destroying a spirit&quot; in Exalted. if you take most Solar Essence 1 Charms, you'll notice they usually address the Solars as the slayers of darkness, and I think GET stands a little apart into that because, well you just slay anything. Since the topic of souls is furthermore quite touchy in fiction, I was wondering if there were insight as to what it means in the world of Exalted to definitively destroy a soul (apparently they are not in limited numbers, but there is the topic of reincarnation, etc ...)<br /> <br /> Do ghosts reappear when slained even if they have no cult ? Or is it just gods and demons that reform only this specific condition ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T09:48:44-07:00","id":1406795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts?p=1406791#post1406791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm looking for insight of the meaning of &quot;definitively destroying a spirit&quot; in Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it's pretty much what it says - it destroys the spirit (which can be more than just ghosts, remember - &quot;spirit&quot; is a broader category of being in Exalted), in such a way that only the very most powerful spirits can continue to exist in <i>any</i> form. Eric's already noted that the slain primordial titans didn't quite die completely, but were rather reduced to the Neverborn. And in 2e, if you used Ghost-Eating Technique to kill a Deathlord, it could still come back, albeit lessened in power, unless you found its secret, unique weakness and used that to <i>permanently</i> kill it. I'd suspect that 3e's treatment of the Deathlords will probably have something like that as well. Similarly, if you used GET on a god at the power level of the Incarnae, to off the Unconquered Sun or something, I'd imagine they'd still come back, in some horrible twisted form. Likewise extremely potent elementals, on the level of the Kukla, the greater elemental dragon of earth from 2e. But any spirit of lesser potency than those ones is just destroyed totally, snuffed from existence. If you slay Ahlat or Ligier or Fakharu or the Prince of the Red Chamber using Ghost-Eating Technique, that spirit is dead, forever.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">if you take most Solar Essence 1 Charms, you'll notice they usually address the Solars as the slayers of darkness, and I think GET stands a little apart into that because, well you just slay anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that while the fluff of the Solar charms may talk about slaying darkness, they are generally not limited to doing that. They'll work just fine on <i>non-</i>darkness too. (The sort-of exception are charms that explicitly target creatures of darkness. But those are relatively rare, and even that category, if you examine it closely, doesn't necessarily equate to &quot;evil&quot;. It's apparently not set by the Unconquered Sun as it was in past editions, so it's not purely subjective, but it still appears to be a basically Creation-centric designation, given to spirits and other supernatural creatures that are basically inimical to Creation. But a creature that spawned in the Wyld and was totally non-sapient, with no ability to choose its actions, just a mad urge to rampage, could probably still be a creature of darkness. So that doesn't really line up with much that modern morality, at least, would call &quot;evil&quot;).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since the topic of souls is furthermore quite touchy in fiction, I was wondering if there were insight as to what it means in the world of Exalted to definitively destroy a soul (apparently they are not in limited numbers, but there is the topic of reincarnation, etc ...)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is one of the questions that Exalted wants you to examine. <i>Is</i> it wrong to permanently kill something, if it could otherwise return to hurt you or innocent people again? To use a real-world analogy, imagine you were in charge of defending a town against wild animal attacks, and you discovered that the last member of a nearly-extinct species was stalking townspeople. You know that now that it's learned to hunt humans, it will likely continue to do so, and even if you just capture it and move it to a wilderness area, you're not really ending the threat to people's lives, just making it a bit more unlikely (plus, if it lives around where the town is, moving it to another location may well mean the extinction of the species anyway, since you're moving it away from the extremely limited breeding pool). What's the right decision? Kill the creature, and defend the lives of the people you're supposed to protect? Or let it live, preserving a species at the potential cost of human lives? That's the kind of moral dilemma that charms like Ghost-Eating Technique exist to foster, and can't if they sugar-coat the effects.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do ghosts reappear when slained even if they have no cult ? Or is it just gods and demons that reform only this specific condition ?</div> </div> </div> </div>3e hasn't given us too much info on ghosts yet. In 2e, every time a ghost was &quot;killed&quot; (again, meaning incapacitated with lethal damage), it vanished, and had a chance of losing some or all of its Passions, the strong emotions that kept it linked to existence. A ghost that lost all its Passions and was killed could go into Lethe, but might also go into Oblivion. Ghosts who had heard the whispers of the Neverborn and been infected by that could treat that as a Passion, preventing them from completely vanishing on death, and if they <i>did</i> finally completely end, they'd almost certainly go into Oblivion. As has been pointed out, in 3e it's just &quot;oblivion&quot;, no Significant Capital Letter. Oblivion is not a cosmic force, it's just the end. But I'd still think that things work in roughly the same way - ghosts will still have passions, the emotions and principles they cling too, and killing them may cause them to let go of those. And we know the whispers of the Neverborn are still a thing, even if, again, there's no capital-W Whispers trait, and I expect that sort of madness will still serve as an attachment for some ghosts too.<br /> <br /> And a cult can probably serve as a connection for a ghost too. It might not be quite as simple as a god or demon's &quot;have a cult, have a chance to resurrect&quot;. Instead, the cult, if it was connected to one of the ghost's passions, might serve as the fetter (the physical representation of the passion), so that destroying the fetter would require finding all the cult members and getting them to stop worshiping the ghost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T10:02:38-07:00","id":1406800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts?p=1406781#post1406781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for the answer.<br /> <br /> Still a few questions about it : Does GET destroys permanently &quot;any&quot; spirit killed by it ? (Gods, demons, elementals, no matter their power). I'm also indecisive in considering this technique is basically evil (it simply and purely destroys a soul, which are apparently in limited number in Creation) or not (it's one of the first Charm of the Solar, usually the good guys, at least when you look the other starter Charms in many abilities). Any advice on how to handle it ?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You always have the option of 'just' beating up a ghost with the pre-req charm spirit cutting attack if you want to beat them up without permanently destroying them. Or make a custom charm that lets them emulate the lunar charms that give you the option to just seal a spirit away in something without destroying it.<br /> <br /> Edit: As for morality, I don't really see how killing any kind of spirit is morally different from anything else you kill (unless your character in game really heavily justifies killing humans by saying 'well they might stick around as ghosts so its not like I definitely completely ended their existence', I guess?) unless your game is running on Creation having limited numbers of souls instead of being able to make new ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 08-07-2020, 01:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T17:34:12-07:00","id":1406863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts?p=1406776#post1406776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">It's some combination of &quot;it's a legend,&quot; &quot;maybe that does mean something if you want it to in your game,&quot; and &quot;it's a core book error.&quot; Take your pick!</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">There's still the bleak depths of the waterways of the Underworld, is there not?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200b</span></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts?p=1406768#post1406768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Lethe is a peaceful transition, and the Solar Exalted already have social tools to ease ghosts along the way.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Hmm, I always read the Zenith Caste Anima as also doing such a thing, but right now...</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts?p=1406781#post1406781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Solar, usually the good guys</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily. Or at least, a give one might only be the good guys to a certain cross section of people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T18:27:34-07:00","id":1406871,"title":"","content":"The Primordial aren\u2019t completely dead even when killed by GET so there are things that it can\u2019t destroy permanently for sure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts?p=1406730#post1406730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Compassion.<br /> <br /> I should even think that being able to tell ghosts that you can skip over everything and send them on if they dig in their heels could help prevent some from being too stubborn about it, if there's a touch of ruthlessness to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are \u201ckilled\u201d either ways so I don\u2019t understand why I need to do it the long and hard way. Though this remind me of how the monk in the White Snake legend is usually seen as cruel and ruthless in modern adaptations when he tries to destroy the yaoguai.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T07:20:40-07:00","id":1407135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts?p=1406871#post1406871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Primordial aren\u2019t completely dead even when killed by GET so there are things that it can\u2019t destroy permanently for sure.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> They are \u201ckilled\u201d either ways so I don\u2019t understand why I need to do it the long and hard way. Though this remind me of how the monk in the White Snake legend is usually seen as cruel and ruthless in modern adaptations when he tries to destroy the yaoguai.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's the whole &quot;treating it like a person and helping them wrap up their final business before going&quot; x &quot;just hit it like the damn pest is and be over with&quot; conundrum wrapped in one's resolution preferences, i guess. but kind of easy to see why some would interpret the later as brutal and ruthless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T07:39:46-07:00","id":1407138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts?p=1406871#post1406871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are \u201ckilled\u201d either ways so I don\u2019t understand why I need to do it the long and hard way.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the sole motive of the character is to remove a ghost from activity, then a quick and pragmatic process without regards for the ghost's personhood is likely to be their main priority.<br /> <br /> If the character views the ghost as a person and treats it as such, they can probably be expected to have an emotional and social motive to ensure that the ghost is satisfied and fulfilled before passing on, their final moments an experience of peace and contentment.<br /> <br /> Not to mention the fact that ghosts are capable of persuading you to do things their way.<br /> <br /> It's much like, when assessing possible deaths for an elderly person who probably doesn't have that much longer to live, the difference between them slipping away quietly and peacefully in their sleep, having last experienced comfortable and familiar surroundings, and going out slowly with their lungs being torn to shreds, hacking, desperately gasping for air in a grim hospital setting that would be terribly impersonal even under circumstances where personnel weren't keeping a distance from them to avoid having or spreading the same fate.<br /> <br /> I mean, we're all dying either way, and yet it appears that the contents and duration of the ensuing life is still a thing that people care about for themselves and one another. Even for those whose deaths are a lot more imminent, hospice care and Make-a-Wish type deals are still a thing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-11T09:29:57-07:00","id":1407533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts?p=1406871#post1406871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are \u201ckilled\u201d either ways so I don\u2019t understand why I need to do it the long and hard way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same reasons why, in the real world, I might honour a last request from an old man on his deathbed despite the fact that he likely won't live to see his request fulfilled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/894-skeptic-tank","name":"Skeptic Tank","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar894_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-11T09:39:38-07:00","id":1407538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Skeptic Tank</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts?p=1407533#post1407533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Same reasons why, in the real world, I might honour a last request from an old man on his deathbed despite the fact that he likely won't live to see his request fulfilled.</div> </div> </div> </div>What would those reasons be?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts?p=1407138#post1407138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If the sole motive of the character is to remove a ghost from activity, then a quick and pragmatic process without regards for the ghost's personhood is likely to be their main priority.<br /> <br /> If the character views the ghost as a person and treats it as such, they can probably be expected to have an emotional and social motive to ensure that the ghost is satisfied and fulfilled before passing on, their final moments an experience of peace and contentment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah yeah, exorcism here in my country usually involves just beating the living crap out of the ghost for Daoism priests and chanting sutra endlessly on the Buddhism side so that it got forced into Samsara again (maybe falling into Diyu, I don\u2019t really know the detail yet). Knowing the ghost\u2019s regret is always useful for such rituals, but not to the extend talking about here.<br /> <br /> Every day that the ghost lingering on this world is a day that they are going against Heaven\u2019s will and thus will gain negative karma so trying to exorcist them asap is seen as a good thing for them unless you want the ghost to be reincarnate as a maggot or worse in the next life, plus there are also enforcers from Diyu (Black and White Impermanence) that are tasked with capturing ghosts and they probably aren\u2019t as nice as a mortal. <br /> <br /> Though I guess there aren\u2019t any negative metaphysical reasons when ghosts don\u2019t enter Samsara in Creation asap so playing a Ghost Detective would be fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 08-11-2020, 12:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-11T13:17:12-07:00","id":1407574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts?p=1407538#post1407538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What would those reasons be?</div> </div> </div> </div>Different reasons for different people.<br /> <br /> Some might do it for a family member, as a way of upholding their family bonds, but might not do it for a stranger.<br /> <br /> Others might do it for a stranger, treating it as an ethical stance - 'you help people when they say they're in need, even if you don't really think it will matter in the long run.'<br /> <br /> Others might have a religious obligation that places the emphasis on the intent of their actions, rather than on the strict result.<br /> <br /> Others might believe that doing something kind for those in need will cause the cosmos to 'pay it forward' somehow.<br /> <br /> Others might see something in the old man that reminds them of someone else they failed to help - and making this effort will help them to deal with the guilt they feel.<br /> <br /> <br /> If it helps, think of a war movie where someone lying with a soon-to-be-fatal wound says &quot;please don't go - I don't want to die alone!&quot; There are always some people who, when push came to shove, might get up and go - this guy's not long for the world, best for me to live for myself! And yet, some people are going to stay with the wounded soldier until the light dies, and might never really be able to articulate why.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/894-skeptic-tank","name":"Skeptic Tank","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar894_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-11T19:45:34-07:00","id":1407648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts?p=1407538#post1407538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah yeah, exorcism here in my country usually involves just beating the living crap out of the ghost for Daoism priests and chanting sutra endlessly on the Buddhism side so that it got forced into Samsara again (maybe falling into Diyu, I don\u2019t really know the detail yet). Knowing the ghost\u2019s regret is always useful for such rituals, but not to the extend talking about here.<br /> <br /> Every day that the ghost lingering on this world is a day that they are going against Heaven\u2019s will and thus will gain negative karma so trying to exorcist them asap is seen as a good thing for them unless you want the ghost to be reincarnate as a maggot or worse in the next life, plus there are also enforcers from Diyu (Black and White Impermanence) that are tasked with capturing ghosts and they probably aren\u2019t as nice as a mortal.<br /> <br /> Though I guess there aren\u2019t any negative metaphysical reasons when ghosts don\u2019t enter Samsara in Creation asap so playing a Ghost Detective would be fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand. And certainly adherents of the Immaculate Philosophy would share that notion that it is for the good of all including the ghost to expediate their passage into Lethe. Given their worldview, I could actually see it in terms of where the ghost's lingering issues are not only irrelevant, but actually conceited. It is not proper conduct for the whole cycle of reincarnation to stop just because of your petty personal issues. Death constitutes the end of your stake in these things, and if you left things out of order when your life ceased you need to face the judgement of the Dragons in determining your next life based on that, not linger against them in the hopes of fixing things up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-11T23:34:00-07:00","id":1407663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Skeptic Tank</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts?p=1407574#post1407574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Different reasons for different people.<br /> <br /> Some might do it for a family member, as a way of upholding their family bonds, but might not do it for a stranger.<br /> <br /> Others might do it for a stranger, treating it as an ethical stance - 'you help people when they say they're in need, even if you don't really think it will matter in the long run.'<br /> <br /> Others might have a religious obligation that places the emphasis on the intent of their actions, rather than on the strict result.<br /> <br /> Others might believe that doing something kind for those in need will cause the cosmos to 'pay it forward' somehow.<br /> <br /> Others might see something in the old man that reminds them of someone else they failed to help - and making this effort will help them to deal with the guilt they feel.<br /> <br /> <br /> If it helps, think of a war movie where someone lying with a soon-to-be-fatal wound says &quot;please don't go - I don't want to die alone!&quot; There are always some people who, when push came to shove, might get up and go - this guy's not long for the world, best for me to live for myself! And yet, some people are going to stay with the wounded soldier until the light dies, and might never really be able to articulate why.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess peacocking to people your virtue for social points is also good thing, and obeying traditions and your elders is always good, plus doing something that has no physical result aside from feeling good is also obviously nice, since it helps fight depression.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts?p=1407648#post1407648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Death constitutes the end of your stake in these things, and if you left things out of order when your life ceased you need to face the judgement of the Dragons in determining your next life based on that, not linger against them in the hopes of fixing things up.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bRight, let karma get to your killer and go back to the cycle of incarnation instead. Does the Realm has anything like karma though?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 08-12-2020, 02:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T03:10:08-07:00","id":1407671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1406170-trying-to-understand-ghosts?p=1407663#post1407663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bRight, let karma get to your killer and go back to the cycle of incarnation instead. Does the Realm has anything like karma though?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you behave well you might be reincarnated as a literal god on earth whose every mortal obey, I guess it's some sort of karma ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}